      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Let $\\alpha = \\cos^2 x.$ Then $\\frac{1}{\\sec x} = \\frac{1 + \\tan x}{\\tan x} = \\tan x + \\frac{1}{\\tan x}$. Since $\\frac{1}{\\sec x} + \\tan x = \\frac{a}{b}$, then $\\tan x + \\frac{1}{\\tan x} = \\frac{a}{b}$. This implies that $a + b = 72$. Since $\\frac{a}{b} = \\sqrt{72}$, then $\\sqrt{72} = 6\\sqrt{2}$, so we have $\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{a(6)}{b(6)} = 6\\sqrt{2}$. Solving for $a$ and $b$, we get $\\boxed{6}$.",
