    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We start by squaring the given equation, \\[\\sec^2 x + 2 \\sec x \\tan x + \\tan^2 x = \\frac{16}{9}.\\] Next, we know that $\\sec^2 x - \\tan^2 x = 1,$ so we substitute this to get \\[\\tan^2 x + 2 \\sec x \\tan x = \\frac{16}{9}.\\] Now, since $\\sin x = \\tan x / \\sec x,$ we have \\[\\sin^2 x + 2 \\sin x = \\frac{16}{9},\\] which is a quadratic in $\\sin x.$ The quadratic factors as \\[(\\sin x - 2)(\\sin x + \\frac{8}{3}) = 0,\\] so the possible values of $\\sin x$ are $\\boxed{\\frac{2}{3} \\text{ or } -\\frac{8}{3}}.$",
